<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore weekly residue down, distillates mixed.</title>
<headline>Singapore weekly residue down, distillates mixed.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore weekly residue stocks plunged by 1.158 million barrels in the week ended November 27 to 9.801 million barrels, Singapore's Trade Development Board (TDB) said.</p>
<p>They include HSFO, LSFO, LSWR and the straight-run atmospheric residue, but exclude bitumen.</p>
<p>Middle-distillate stocks fell by a marginal 64,000 barrels to 8.302 million barrels. Middle distillates comprise jet, kerosene and gas oil.</p>
<p>Light distillate stocks rose by 1.464 million barrels to 6.624 million barrels. They comprise gasoline, reformate and naphtha.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
